  "hints": [
    "Read row by row, the matrix is one long sorted list.",
    "Binary search over positions `0 .. rows*cols - 1`, mapping position `p` to `matrix[p / cols][p % cols]`.",
    "lo, hi = 0, rows*cols - 1\nwhile lo <= hi:\n    mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n    v = matrix[mid // cols][mid % cols]\n    if v == target: return true\n    if v < target: lo = mid + 1\n    else: hi = mid - 1\nreturn false",
    "Treating the matrix as a flattened sorted array gives O(log(m n))."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(log(m n))",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
